{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Ashur</b> — for it is written, \"and Ashur is his king.\" He does not rely on Ashur, nor on our horses brought from Egypt." "<b>nor will we say again, 'Our Elohim,' to the work of our hands</b> — corresponding to the work of craftsmen. For there is no one to help one who has no strength, like the orphan — only You. And it is written: \"Father of orphans.\" And this corresponds to, \"for you have stumbled in your iniquity,\" and there is none to help you."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites Hosea's own earlier words (Hosea 10:6 or similar) as the background for the repentance expressed in 14:4.", 1 "The phrase 'and there is none to help you' may allude to the same verse about the orphan; the syntax of the final clause is compressed and possibly elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:14.429980393Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}